  "summary": "Done. Everything builds; all four test projects pass (6 + 8 + 83 unit/subcutaneous, 20 integration against a real PostgreSQL container).\n\n**PostgreSQL**\n- `Directory.Packages.props` / `CleanArchitecture.Infrastructure.csproj`: added `Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL`; added `Testcontainers.PostgreSql` for the integration-test project.\n- `Infrastructure/DependencyInjection.cs`: `AddPersistence` now takes `IConfiguration` and uses `UseNpgsql(configuration.GetConnectionString(\"DefaultConnection\"))`.\n- `appsettings.json` gained an empty `ConnectionStrings:DefaultConnection`; `appsettings.Development.json` holds the local value (`Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=tutorialsdb;Username=postgres;Password=postgres`).\n- Deleted the two SQLite migrations and `src/CleanArchitecture.Api/CleanArchitecture.sqlite`; generated a fresh `20261028114456_InitialCreate` against Npgsql.\n- `RequestPipeline.ApplyMigrations()` (called from `Program.cs`) runs `Database.Migrate()` on startup, guarded by `IsNpgsql()` so the SQLite-backed subcutaneous tests still build their schema from the model.\n- Integration tests: `SqliteTestDatabase` replaced by `PostgresTestDatabase` (Testcontainers `postgres`, database `tutorialsdb`), `WebAppFactory` starts it in `InitializeAsync` and resets with `EnsureDeleted` + `Migrate`.\n- Added `.env.example` with `POSTGRES_DB/USER/PASSWORD/PORT` and the container connection string, since `docker-compose.yml` sources them from env.\n\n**Categories**\n- New `Domain/Categories/Category.cs`; `Tutorial` gained an optional `CategoryId` (constructor + `Update`).\n- New `ICategoriesRepository`, `CreateCategoryCommand(+Handler, Validator)`, `ListCategoriesQuery(+Handler)`, `CategoriesRepository`, `CategoryConfigurations`, `Categories` DbSet, and a nullable FK on `Tutorials` (`OnDelete: SetNull`).\n- `GET /api/categories` and `POST /api/categories` via a new `CategoriesController` returning `{ id, name }` exactly as the contract spells it.\n- `CreateTutorialRequest` / `UpdateTutorialRequest` take an optional `categoryId`; `TutorialResponse` returns `categoryId`. Both tutorial handlers return `404` when the given category does not exist. No other tutorial contract field changed, and `published` still defaults to `false` when the POST body omits it (covered by a new test).\n- Tests added: category create/list subcutaneous tests, tutorial-with-category and unknown-category 404 cases (subcutaneous + integration), and a category badge/`categoryId` round-trip through the API.\n\nInterpretation taken: tutorials are still filtered server-side by `title` only — the contract shows no category query parameter, and its note says the UI matches categories to tutorials client-side.\n\nTwo items I could not do here: `docker-compose.yml` (postgres service, named volume, env-driven credentials, dropping the sqlite bind-mount) and `README.md` (start-the-database / run-the-API commands) both fall outside the paths this run is permitted to modify, so they remain unchanged. The Category dropdown, list badge, and category filter are frontend work and belong to the other repository.",
