    "notes": "All ids are GUIDs serialized as JSON strings (not numbers) — `id` and `categoryId` are always string-typed, so the UI's strict-equality match on category.id === tutorial.categoryId works as long as it never coerces to number. `categoryId` is nullable and may be omitted/null. Route ids are constrained to :guid, so a non-GUID id yields 404. JSON is camelCase; createdAt/updatedAt are ISO-8601 date-time strings. Every endpoint the frontend contract listed is implemented. Differences from the received contract: POST /tutorials returns the full created tutorial (not an empty body) with a Location header; DELETE /tutorials (all) returns {\"message\": \"...\"} rather than an empty body; `published` IS accepted on POST /tutorials and defaults to false when omitted. Errors use ProblemDetails. CORS is enabled for the frontend origin; API listens on http://localhost:5001."
